Unicorn Horns are, IMO, vastly overrated as weapons.  In the early
game, you'd be far better off with a Dwarvish Short Sword and a small
shield than a 2-handed weapon.  Once you're in the midgame and have
(hopefully) found an altar, you can switch to whatever your God gives
you, and you won't have wasted skill points on both Dagger AND Unicorn
Horn.  At least Dagger has some potential use late-game - for throwing
- but Unicorn Horn is just a complete waste of skill points.

Someone recently mentioned that a maxed-out Crysknife is actually just
as good as many artifact weapons in terms of basic damage potential,
and long worms certainly aren't uncommon or hard to kill.

